.TH CCOPS 1 2026-11-11 "ccops 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccops \- a small host inventory CLI built with cliforge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccops
[\fIflags\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ccops keeps a list of hosts in a JSON file. Data goes to stdout, diagnostics to stderr, every change has \-\-dry\-run, and destructive changes ask on a terminal and refuse without one unless \-\-yes is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ccops hosts list
list hosts, optionally filtered
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fIENV\fR
only hosts in this environment
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
only hosts with this role
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fISTATE\fR
only hosts in this state
.RE
.TP
.B ccops hosts show \fINAME\fR
show one host
.TP
.B ccops hosts add \fINAME\fR
add a host; repeating the same add changes nothing
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fIENV\fR
environment, such as prod
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIROLE\fR
role, such as web or db
.TP
\fB\-\-ip\fR \fIIP\fR
IPv4 or IPv6 address
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fISTATE\fR
lifecycle state (default active)
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\fR \fITAG\fR
a tag; repeat for several
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print what would change and change nothing
.RE
.TP
.B ccops hosts remove \fINAME...\fR
remove hosts; asks first, refuses without a terminal unless \-\-yes
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-missing\-ok\fR
exit 0 when a host is already absent
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
print what would change and change nothing
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
confirm without asking (required when stdin is not a terminal)
.RE
.TP
.B ccops config
print the effective settings; \-\-explain shows where each came from
.RS
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
show the source of every value: flag, env, file or default
.RE
.TP
.B ccops completion \fISHELL\fR
print a Bash completion script
.TP
.B ccops man
print the man page (roff)
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFORMAT\fR
output format (env CCOPS_OUTPUT, config output, default text)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
same as \-\-output json: one JSON document on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIWHEN\fR
colour: auto, always or never; auto is off when NO_COLOR is set or stdout is not a terminal (env CCOPS_COLOR, config color, default auto)
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-inventory\fR \fIPATH\fR
inventory file (env CCOPS_INVENTORY, config inventory, default inventory.json)
.TP
\fB\-\-lock\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR
seconds to wait for another writer's lock (env CCOPS_LOCK_TIMEOUT, config lock_timeout, default 5)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
config file (env CCOPS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/ccops/config)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
print only what a pipe needs: no notes, names only in lists
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
print debug diagnostics on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show this help and exit 0
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
print the version and exit 0
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CCOPS_OUTPUT
output format; overrides the config file, overridden by \-\-output. An empty value counts as unset.
.TP
.B CCOPS_COLOR
colour: auto, always or never; auto is off when NO_COLOR is set or stdout is not a terminal; overrides the config file, overridden by \-\-color. An empty value counts as unset.
.TP
.B CCOPS_INVENTORY
inventory file; overrides the config file, overridden by \-\-inventory. An empty value counts as unset.
.TP
.B CCOPS_LOCK_TIMEOUT
seconds to wait for another writer's lock; overrides the config file, overridden by \-\-lock\-timeout. An empty value counts as unset.
.TP
.B CCOPS_CONFIG
path of the config file; overridden by \-\-config.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
when set to a non\-empty value, color auto turns colour off; color always still turns it on (https://no\-color.org).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ccops/config
key = value lines, # comments; keys: output, color, inventory, lock_timeout. $XDG_CONFIG_HOME replaces ~/.config. Relative paths in it are relative to the file.
.TP
.I inventory.json
the default inventory; written atomically (temporary file, fsync, rename) under an flock on inventory.json.lock
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
ok: the command did what was asked, or there was nothing to do
.TP
.B 1
failure: the command ran and failed: unreadable data, a conflict, a lock timeout
.TP
.B 2
usage: the invocation was wrong: unknown command or flag, bad value, bad config file
.TP
.B 3
not found: a named object does not exist
.TP
.B 4
refused: a destructive change was not confirmed
.TP
.B 130
interrupted: Ctrl\-C (128 + SIGINT)
.TP
.B 141
broken pipe: the reader of stdout went away (128 + SIGPIPE)
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ccops hosts list \-\-env prod
ccops hosts list \-\-json | jq \-r '.hosts[].ip'
ccops hosts show web\-1 \-\-json
ccops hosts add web\-3 \-\-env prod \-\-role web \-\-ip 10.0.1.13 \-\-dry\-run
ccops hosts remove web\-3 \-\-dry\-run
ccops hosts remove web\-3 \-\-yes
ccops config \-\-explain
ccops config > ~/.config/ccops/config
source <(ccops completion bash)
ccops man > ccops.1 && man ./ccops.1
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccops (1) \-\-help, \fBccops completion bash\fR
